From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:00:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: MADEIRA_FEX_BATCH2=1, four transition and backpatch
 items on iOS, off by default

MADEIRA_FEX_BATCH2=1 sets IosFexBatch2 (Arm64Emitter.h) at process init,
less the items MADEIRA_FEX_BATCH2_SKIP names (comma-separated), so a
failing batch can be bisected:

alias: x64->EC translation by one probe. The writer keeps every listed
image's 64 KB granules in IosAliasGranules (32768 slots, linear
probing, at most half full), under IosAliasGen: granule + 1 and the
image's JitBase - PeBase, or a part marker when the granule is not all
one image's. ExitFunctionEC and ExitFunctionECJit probe it before the
hint and walk: an empty slot means no image (the target stays), a whole
granule read with the count even and unmoved adds the delta, anything
else takes the walk. RDR2 makes about 520,000 x64->EC calls a second
and the table holds about 460 entries, retired ones included, walked
newest-first behind a one-entry hint. A retire rebuilds the table; on
overflow the lookup turns itself off. The log says
"FEX: batch2 bits=... alias-granules=N".

ffs: ExitToX64's FFS bypass branches to the pool copy the target was
found in, not to its PE VA, which reached the copy through a Mach
exec-fault redirect (about 33 us).

dmb: enter_jit drops its DMB ISH between the InSimulation store and the
sweep gate read, about 520,000 times a second. The sweeper, once per
code generation, calls NtFlushProcessWriteBuffers between its gate
store and its InSimulation reads: Wine iOS reads every thread's
registers there, which takes each through a barrier, the asymmetric
form of the same handshake.

uabp: HandleUnalignedAccess takes the backpatch lock and stores the
patched instructions through the RW alias; through the RX view each
store and the CAS was a Mach exception Wine emulated.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-batch2.md
Offered-upstream: no; Madeira's iOS code
